{"title":"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two straight lines intersect as shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The measure of the angle marked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/febf4307ef5db5cad13686c742d8a3c43eb2a1cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed { }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f82202c2a1e926c908cf11f915220e886875e82a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 60^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 120^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 30^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 300^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"499\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b49fcb2f74ccae5ec0e722a8c65b5b9bbd93720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> degrees and the missing angle forms a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Straight_angle\" title=\"Straight angle\">straight angle</a>, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/7/597cb969597f1443acbc2e83f634c5fcc4308ef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^{\\circ} + \\boxed { } = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/173d50b051c5277eb1d01dddcad4296b8b4e199c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed { } = \\boxed {{\\textbf (A) }  60^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"103\" height=\"32\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> angle and the missing angle are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertical_angle&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Vertical angle (page does not exist)\">vertical angles</a>, they are equal to each other.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/173d50b051c5277eb1d01dddcad4296b8b4e199c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed { } = \\boxed {{\\textbf (A) }  60^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"103\" height=\"32\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems